  offerLine: Here's a business idea. You put lanterns out. Moths come to the lanterns. I come to the moths. Everyone's happy, except the moths. Two lanterns ought to do it.
  activeLine: Two lanterns out where they can be seen, then close up and let's see who turns up.
  readyLine: Look at them all! I haven't eaten this well in years. I strung up some of my good thread in thanks. Don't ask about the little lights. I don't know how they work.
  doneLine: One last thing. It's a bit of a stretch.
